### Honor an explicitly empty WallpaperPath

**Severity:** `medium`

With a nonempty `Multimon.WallpaperPath` configured, passing `-WallpaperPath ''` currently selects that configured folder instead of the documented generated-color-bar mode: `Get-MultimonSetting` treats an empty override as absent. Handle the explicitly bound empty value at this callsite, leaving omitted arguments, whitespace-only overrides, nonempty paths, and all other helper callers on their existing resolution path. PowerShell converts an explicitly bound null to an empty string, so it selects the same generated mode.

```suggestion
$wallpaperSource = if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('WallpaperPath') -and $WallpaperPath -ceq '') {
    ''
} else {
    Get-MultimonSetting -Configuration $configuration -Name 'WallpaperPath' -Override $WallpaperPath -Default ''
}
```
